#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Courses and tutorials {#courses-and-tutorials}"
msgstr "Kursus dan tutorial {#courses-and-tutorials}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recommended learning material for developing quantum teams. Below are brief "
"learning outcomes and intended audiences for each learning asset. Follow the"
" links for more details on each.\n"
msgstr ""
"Materi pembelajaran yang direkomendasikan untuk mengembangkan tim kuantum. "
"Di bawah ini adalah hasil pembelajaran singkat dan audiens yang dituju untuk"
" setiap aset pembelajaran. Ikuti link untuk detail lebih lanjut tentang "
"masing-masing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Quantum business foundations](/learning/courses/quantum-business-foundations):** \n"
"* Audience: Accessible to anyone. Ideal for raising awareness across the broader institution, possibly not necessary for core team.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Familiarity with quantum computing terminology, the state of the science, and awareness of a few application areas and areas of potential business value.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Dasar-dasar bisnis kuantum](/learning/courses/quantum-business-foundations):**\n"
"* Audiens: Dapat diakses oleh siapa saja. Ideal untuk meningkatkan kesadaran di seluruh institusi yang lebih luas, mungkin tidak diperlukan untuk tim inti.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Keakraban dengan terminologi komputasi kuantum, keadaan ilmu pengetahuan, dan kesadaran tentang beberapa area aplikasi dan area nilai bisnis potensial.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Basics of quantum information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information):**\n"
"* Audience: Those seeking a deep theoretical foundation for quantum computing: students and early career scientists.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Theoretical foundations of classical and quantum information, ability to describe quantum systems using linear algebra, describe multi-qubit systems and entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Dasar-dasar informasi kuantum](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information):**\n"
"* Audiens: Mereka yang mencari fondasi teoritis yang mendalam untuk komputasi kuantum: mahasiswa dan ilmuwan awal karier.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Fondasi teoritis informasi klasik dan kuantum, kemampuan untuk mendeskripsikan sistem kuantum menggunakan aljabar linier, mendeskripsikan sistem multi-Qubit dan keterikatan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Quantum diagonalization algorithms](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms):** \n"
"* Audience: Those with strong quantum and computing backgrounds seeking to understand prominent and promising algorithms.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Familiarity with algorithms like VQE, SQD, and SKQD, explain how different algorithms' costs scale with variables like problem size and the number of groups of commuting Pauli operators, and how to choose a good approach.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Algoritma diagonalisasi kuantum](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms):**\n"
"* Audiens: Mereka dengan latar belakang kuantum dan komputasi yang kuat yang ingin memahami algoritma yang menonjol dan menjanjikan.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Keakraban dengan algoritma seperti VQE, SQD, dan SKQD, menjelaskan bagaimana biaya berbagai algoritma menskalakan dengan variabel seperti ukuran masalah dan jumlah kelompok operator Pauli yang saling berkomutasi, dan cara memilih pendekatan yang baik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to these self-guided courses, many tutorials on IBM Quantum&reg;"
" Platform showcase the latest algorithms and most powerful methods. "
"Tutorials tend to be shorter assets, showing a streamlined implementation of"
" a method. Here are a few of particular interest.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain kursus-kursus yang dipandu sendiri ini, banyak tutorial di IBM "
"Quantum&reg; Platform yang menampilkan algoritma terbaru dan metode paling "
"ampuh. Tutorial cenderung menjadi aset yang lebih pendek, menampilkan "
"implementasi streamline dari suatu metode. Berikut beberapa yang sangat "
"menarik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[CHSH inequality](/tutorials/chsh-inequality):** \n"
"* Audience: For users fairly new to quantum computing. \n"
"* Learning outcomes: There are quantum correlations that are stronger than classical physics can explain, familiarity running a job using Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Pertidaksamaan CHSH](/tutorials/chsh-inequality):**\n"
"* Audiens: Untuk pengguna yang cukup baru mengenal komputasi kuantum.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Ada korelasi kuantum yang lebih kuat dari yang bisa dijelaskan fisika klasik, keakraban menjalankan job menggunakan Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Sample-based quantum diagonalization of a chemistry Hamiltonian](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization):** \n"
"* Audience: Those with strong quantum and computing backgrounds seeking to understand prominent and promising algorithms.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: How to use an SQD approach to find the ground state energy of a chemical system.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Diagonalisasi kuantum berbasis sampel dari Hamiltonian kimia](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization):**\n"
"* Audiens: Mereka dengan latar belakang kuantum dan komputasi yang kuat yang ingin memahami algoritma yang menonjol dan menjanjikan.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Cara menggunakan pendekatan SQD untuk menemukan energi ground state dari sistem kimia.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization of a fermionic lattice model](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization):** \n"
"* Audience: Those with strong quantum and computing backgrounds seeking to understand prominent and promising algorithms.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Use the Krylov method from linear algebra, combine the speed of SQD with convergence guarantees from the Krylov method, know the conditions for convergence guarantees.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Diagonalisasi kuantum Krylov berbasis sampel dari model kisi fermionik](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization):**\n"
"* Audiens: Mereka dengan latar belakang kuantum dan komputasi yang kuat yang ingin memahami algoritma yang menonjol dan menjanjikan.\n"
"* Hasil pembelajaran: Gunakan metode Krylov dari aljabar linier, kombinasikan kecepatan SQD dengan jaminan konvergensi dari metode Krylov, ketahui kondisi untuk jaminan konvergensi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are many other courses and tutorials available on [IBM Quantum "
"Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/). Check it out to see all the "
"latest content!\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada banyak kursus dan tutorial lain yang tersedia di [IBM Quantum "
"Platform](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/). Cek untuk melihat semua konten "
"terbaru!\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Technical development best practices {#technical-development-best-practices}"
msgstr ""
"Praktik terbaik pengembangan teknis {#technical-development-best-practices}"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Follow dev/ops best practices such as CI/CD\n"
msgstr "Ikuti praktik terbaik dev/ops seperti CI/CD\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Develop incrementally, using agile methodology to scale up a technical "
"approach and project\n"
msgstr ""
"Kembangkan secara bertahap, menggunakan metodologi agile untuk menskalakan "
"pendekatan teknis dan proyek\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use simulators for debugging and benchmarking (Do not rely on simulators for"
" too long in proof-of-concept (POC) work; they will not scale to utility)\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan simulator untuk debugging dan benchmarking (Jangan terlalu lama "
"mengandalkan simulator dalam pekerjaan proof-of-concept (POC); simulator "
"tidak akan menskalakan ke utilitas)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reach out to [IBM Quantum Technical support](/guides/support) via the [IBM "
"Cloud Support Center](https://cloud.ibm.com/unifiedsupport/cases/form) for "
"assistance with general technical support inquiries \n"
msgstr ""
"Hubungi [dukungan teknis IBM Quantum](/guides/support) melalui [IBM Cloud "
"Support Center](https://cloud.ibm.com/unifiedsupport/cases/form) untuk "
"bantuan dengan pertanyaan dukungan teknis umum\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use software features such as [Qiskit addons](/guides/addons) and [Qiskit "
"Functions](/guides/functions) to fast-track technical development, learning,"
" and discovery\n"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan fitur software seperti [addon Qiskit](/guides/addons) dan [Qiskit "
"Functions](/guides/functions) untuk mempercepat pengembangan teknis, "
"pembelajaran, dan penemuan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the most out of quantum computing resources**\n"
msgstr "**Manfaatkan sumber daya komputasi kuantum secara maksimal**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum computer access is a precious resource. It is important that "
"technical practitioners use their allocated QPU time, and that they use it "
"wisely. We recommend establishing expected good technical practices that "
"ensure your team is using real quantum computers, scaling problems "
"responsibly, and allocating time appropriately. \n"
msgstr ""
"Akses komputer kuantum adalah sumber daya yang berharga. Penting bahwa "
"praktisi teknis menggunakan waktu QPU yang dialokasikan, dan menggunakannya "
"dengan bijak. Kami menyarankan untuk menetapkan praktik teknis yang baik "
"yang memastikan timmu menggunakan komputer kuantum nyata, menskalakan "
"masalah secara bertanggung jawab, dan mengalokasikan waktu dengan tepat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We recommend starting with small test problems, and increasing to the full-"
"scale problem of interest in a few steps. This is important for reasons "
"beyond resource allocation. \n"
msgstr ""
"Kami menyarankan untuk mulai dengan masalah uji kecil, dan meningkat ke "
"masalah skala penuh yang diminati dalam beberapa langkah. Ini penting karena"
" alasan di luar alokasi sumber daya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As IBM&reg; quantum computers are becoming more powerful, results become "
"increasingly difficult to check with classical computers. Indeed, no "
"classical simulator can exactly simulate all functionality of a modern IBM "
"quantum computer with over 100 qubits. \n"
msgstr ""
"Karena komputer kuantum IBM&reg; semakin canggih, hasil menjadi semakin "
"sulit untuk diperiksa dengan komputer klasik. Memang, tidak ada simulator "
"klasik yang dapat mensimulasikan dengan tepat semua fungsionalitas komputer "
"kuantum IBM modern dengan lebih dari 100 Qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the era of useful quantum computing, the role of simulators is mostly "
"limited to debugging code. Benchmarking with smaller versions of your "
"problem is one alternative when classical confirmation is no longer "
"feasible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di era komputasi kuantum yang berguna, peran simulator sebagian besar "
"terbatas pada debugging kode. Benchmarking dengan versi yang lebih kecil "
"dari masalahmu adalah salah satu alternatif ketika konfirmasi klasik tidak "
"lagi layak.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In many cases, the scaling of your problem may be obvious, such as scaling a"
" machine learning problem by increasing, for example, the number of data "
"points, or the number of features. Another example is the scaling of quantum"
" chemistry problems. It would be prudent for a technical practitioner to run"
" example calculations on small molecules before tackling larger, more "
"interesting systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam banyak kasus, penskalaan masalahmu mungkin jelas, seperti menskalakan "
"masalah machine learning dengan meningkatkan, misalnya, jumlah titik data, "
"atau jumlah fitur. Contoh lain adalah penskalaan masalah kimia kuantum. Akan"
" bijaksana bagi praktisi teknis untuk menjalankan perhitungan contoh pada "
"molekul kecil sebelum menangani sistem yang lebih besar dan lebih menarik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A workflow for scaling up a quantum "
"calculations.](/learning/images/courses/designing-and-leading-quantum-"
"projects/standing-up-team/scaling.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Alur kerja untuk menskalakan perhitungan "
"kuantum.](/learning/images/courses/designing-and-leading-quantum-"
"projects/standing-up-team/scaling.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next lessons, we address promoting your team's abilities to outside "
"groups. Depending on your organization, this might mean grant writing and "
"bringing in collaborators, or it might mean selling your services to "
"clients.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran berikutnya, kita akan membahas mempromosikan kemampuan timmu"
" ke kelompok luar. Tergantung organisasimu, ini mungkin berarti penulisan "
"hibah dan mendatangkan kolaborator, atau mungkin berarti menjual jasamu ke "
"klien.\n"
